WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.430
Good morning, John. First things first, Project
for Awesome is coming and it's coming fast!

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.149
Project for Awesome will be a little bit different
this year and it will take place almost exclusively

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:12.190
on Youtube.com. So if you want to participate
at all, even if you're just tuning in for

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:20.090
a little bit, you need to go right now to
Youtube.com/p4a and subscribe. Right now.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.140
It is extremely important to the success of
the Project for Awesome that you do that.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.380
Once again, right now. However many views
this video gets, that is how many people I

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.460
expect to be subscribed to Youtube.com/p4a!
People, this is for charity!

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.410
Now, if you are going to make a video you
also need to go subscribe to Youtube.com/p4a,

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.110
but you should also go to the links in my
pants to get the thumbnail! Now, only partners

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.690
can change their thumbnail. If you're not
a partner you can't change your thumbnail.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.480
That's fine - you can still participate in
the project - but you should put "Project

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.980
for Awesome" or "P4A" in the title of your
video, and put both of those things in the

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.960
tags, so that we can find your Project for
Awesome video! You must then upload those

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:57.840
videos at noon on December 17th and then throughout
the 17th and 18th, the Project for Awesome

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.390
crew, including John and I, will be featuring
those videos all over the place - on Projectforawesome.com,

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:09.050
on our mailing list, on the front page of
Youtube, and at Youtube.com/p4a.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:12.800
Now, on Wednesday I was in Washington, D.C.,
and when we go places, we do Thoughts from

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:13.800
Places.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.600
Good morning John, I woke up this morning
at 6 a.m., and then at 6:30, and then again

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.560
at 7:30 because apparently (and I guess somewhat
unsurprisingly) Washington, D.C. must have

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.060
more trash than any other city on the planet!
But then the garbage trucks stopped coming

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:35.260
and I woke up blissfully at around 10 a.m.,
dramatically entered my fancy-though-somewhat-tiny

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.820
hotel room, turned off Simplynoise.com, which
helped me sleep but failed to drown out the

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.850
garbage trucks, and then I took a shower from
a shower head that looked remarkably like

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:45.180
the planetary defense system that the crew
of the starship Enterprise had to battle in

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.570
the second season of Star Trek TNG. It totally
freaked me out - I was afraid it was going

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.370
to put me in a stasis field - and then I noticed
this mirror. And then I noticed this mirror.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:57.310
And I notice that there's a hinge on one of
them. And I was trying to figure out why this

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:05.310
mirror had a hinge and I realized it's so
you can do this. They pretty much thought

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:09.110
of everything here at this hotel. And then
I dramatically left my hotel because apparently

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:14.400
my hotel has a thing for curtains, and then
I was released onto the streets of Washington,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.069
D.C. I enjoyed my walk, seeing many monuments
of monumental people. This here is Horis Trinkleton,

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:23.280
the famous cabbage fancier, and here we have
Inglebert Humart, who triumphed at the battle

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.980
of Upper Little Bigton, and then I wandered
past the giant temple to Pescandruscus, the

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:33.130
Zoroastrian god of penetration, and finally
we have the monument of Anjou Teleteleteleton,

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:38.370
the inventor of both velcro and the pencil
sharpener. And then by random chance I ran

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.410
into Quizzuckle Couleasy Flip, the squirrel
ambassador to the United States. We had a

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:46.650
brief conversation in which he apologized
for the crimes of Scuzzy Kazoozle, and informed

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.690
me that since the passage of the Squirrel
Friendliness and Cleanliness Act of 1982,

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.140
there has been a dramatic decrease in squirrel-related
fatalities.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:58.900
So a little-known fact: the squirrels will
only approach humans for two things: food

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.069
and to be on Youtube.

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:04.599
Ok, seriously, though, Washington, D.C. really
is an amazing place. It's a place where you

00:03:04.599 --> 00:03:10.410
feel the power of our nation's past much more
viscerally. I was in D.C. for a little event

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:15.620
thingy that Youtube was throwing for policy
and politics people. I was on a panel about

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:18.880
using Youtube for good in which I talked all
about the Project for Awesome, of course.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.450
It was fun, but way too short, and I wish
I had taken some video of the amazing Indian

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.450
food I got.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.780
John, I'll see you on Monday.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:31.500
Don't forget to go to Youtube.com/p4a and
subscribe! You can do that right now! That's

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.530
the only thing I'm devoting this end screen
to! P4A Youtube.com/p4a go subscribe right

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.379
now! You can also subscribe to get email updates.
That is probably a good idea as well. You

00:03:40.379 --> 00:03:41.989
will not regret this decision.

